<div class="page-header">
  <div>
    <h1>Amazon Seller Tax Readiness</h1>
    <p class="muted">Connect Amazon to import a tax year automatically, clean up tax categories, and generate year-end files for your CPA or TurboTax.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="actions">
    <%= link_to "Upload a file", new_amazon_import_batch_path, class: "button secondary" %>
    <%= link_to "Open tax packet", tax_packet_path(year: @year), class: "button secondary" %>
    <%= link_to "Open TurboTax export", turbo_tax_export_path(year: @year), class: "button secondary" %>
  </div>
</div>

<%= render "amazon_connection", connection: @amazon_connection, latest_sync: @latest_sync, sync_year_options: @sync_year_options %>

<div class="card guide-card" style="margin-bottom:18px;">
  <h2 style="margin-top:0;">How to use this app</h2>
  <p class="guide-copy">
    Work left to right: import Amazon data, review the categories this app suggests, then generate the tax packet or TurboTax export for the selected tax year.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="grid guide-grid cards">
  <div class="card guide-card">
    <div class="guide-step">1</div>
    <h3>Import Amazon data</h3>
    <p class="guide-copy">Connect your Amazon seller account and sync a tax year, or upload a settlement CSV/TSV or 2025 transaction report from Seller Central. Each transaction is split into tax review rows.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card guide-card">
    <div class="guide-step">2</div>
    <h3>Review the queue</h3>
    <p class="guide-copy">Open each import and accept rows that belong in your tax summary. Change the category first when Amazon fees, FBA fees, refunds, shipping, or advertising need correction.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card guide-card">
    <div class="guide-step">3</div>
    <h3>Finish manual inputs</h3>
    <p class="guide-copy">Amazon files do not know what you paid for inventory. Add COGS and business details on the TurboTax export page before treating the final numbers as ready.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card guide-card">
    <div class="guide-step">4</div>
    <h3>Export tax-ready files</h3>
    <p class="guide-copy">Use the tax packet for CPA review, or download the TXF and audit CSV for TurboTax Desktop after rows are categorized and warnings are clear.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="grid cards">
  <div class="card"><div class="muted">Rows needing review</div><div class="value"><%= @pending_review_count %></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="muted">Uncategorized rows</div><div class="value"><%= @uncategorized_count %></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="muted"><%= @year %> accepted rows</div><div class="value"><%= @accepted_count %></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="muted">Excluded rows</div><div class="value"><%= @excluded_count %></div></div>
</div>

<div class="grid cards" style="margin-top:12px;">
  <div class="card"><div class="muted"><%= @year %> gross sales</div><div class="value"><%= number_to_currency(@year_totals.fetch("gross_sales", 0) / 100.0) %></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="muted"><%= @year %> fees</div><div class="value"><%= number_to_currency((@year_totals.fetch("amazon_fees", 0) + @year_totals.fetch("fba_fees", 0)) / 100.0) %></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="muted"><%= @year %> refunds</div><div class="value"><%= number_to_currency(@year_totals.fetch("refunds_returns", 0) / 100.0) %></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="muted">Manual COGS</div><div class="value"><%= @export_input.cost_of_goods_sold_cents.zero? ? "Missing" : number_to_currency(@export_input.cost_of_goods_sold_cents / 100.0) %></div></div>
</div>

<div class="grid dashboard-main">
  <div class="card">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0;">What needs attention</h2>
    <table class="tight">
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Import status</th>
          <td>
            <% if @latest_batch.present? %>
              Latest import: <%= @latest_batch.filename %> from <%= l(@latest_batch.imported_at, format: :short) %>
            <% else %>
              No Amazon data imported yet.
            <% end %>
          </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Review queue</th>
          <td><%= @pending_review_count.zero? ? "No rows waiting for review." : "#{@pending_review_count} rows still need review." %></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">Category cleanup</th>
          <td><%= @uncategorized_count.zero? ? "No uncategorized rows are blocking tax prep." : "#{@uncategorized_count} rows still need a tax category." %></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">COGS input</th>
          <td><%= @export_input.cost_of_goods_sold_cents.zero? ? "Add inventory and purchase totals before final TXF export." : "Manual COGS inputs are on file for #{@year}." %></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Recent imports</h2>
    <table class="tight">
      <thead><tr><th>Import</th><th>Imported</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @recent_batches.each do |batch| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= link_to batch.filename, amazon_import_batch_path(batch) %></td>
            <td><%= l(batch.imported_at, format: :short) %></td>
            <td><%= batch.status.humanize %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <% if @recent_batches.empty? %>
          <tr><td colspan="3">No imports yet.</td></tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
